# The fourth nav scene, and the ONLY one of the four kept out of git. Its three siblings
# -- nav_hospital, nav_office, nav_warehouse -- are tracked at 518 lines each; this one is
# 44 lines, because the scene pipeline was never run on it. No joint drives, no wheel
# colliders, no camera_nav. `nav/tools/run_sync_study.sh` and `run_bounded_study.sh` both
# name it as the leading suspect for the 36 km and 51 km path lengths two outdoor episodes
# recorded, and for the 17.9 km `outdoor_pillars` blow-up in the baseline profile's
# caveats.
#
# Committing it is the worse option in both directions: it would sit beside three working
# scenes under a matching name with nothing marking it as a stub, and it references the
# TIC-VLA submodule by absolute path, so on anyone else's machine it resolves to nothing.
# Rebuild it with `nav/sim/build_nav_scene.sh outdoor_small` when the pipeline is fixed;
# until then the outdoor 1/6 result should be read as a scene problem, not a policy one.
assets/usd/nav_outdoor_small.usda
